# Architecture Rules

- Keep architecture modular and layered.
- Renderer depends only on RHI interfaces.
- Engine core must never directly depend on DirectX 12 APIs.
- DX12 implementation details belong only in backend layer.
- Avoid tight coupling between systems.
- Prefer composition over inheritance unless polymorphism is required.
- Keep public interfaces minimal and stable.
- Avoid cyclic dependencies.
- Use dependency inversion where beneficial.
- Avoid Singleton unless explicitly requested.
- Favor explicit ownership semantics.
- Avoid global mutable state.
- Design systems for long-term maintainability.
- Think carefully before changing architecture.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions.
- Prefer simple and understandable solutions.